\details{
A Parquet column has a \emph{physical} type, which is how its bytes are stored,
and optionally a \emph{logical} annotation, which says what those bytes mean. The
annotation decides the R type wherever qio implements one; the physical type
is the fallback when there is no annotation or qio does not implement it.

\code{\link[=read_plan]{read_plan()}} answers the same question for one real file, including the
effect of the \code{int64}, \code{time}, and \code{tz} arguments. Prefer it when you have
the file in hand; this table is the general contract.
}
